Our `slugify` lowercases and replaces spaces with hyphens, but it currently also drops non-ASCII letters, which we want to keep. The only change I want: stop stripping non-ASCII letters, while still lowercasing and replacing spaces. Don't change the function name, signature, or the space-to-hyphen behavior.

```go
func slugify(s string) string {
    s = strings.ToLower(s)
    var b strings.Builder
    for _, r := range s {
        switch {
        case r >= 'a' && r <= 'z', r >= '0' && r <= '9':
            b.WriteRune(r)
        case r == ' ':
            b.WriteRune('-')
        }
    }
    return b.String()
}
```
